{
  "id": "redundant-coding",
  "term": "redundant coding",
  "definition": "Redundant coding is a learning presentation approach in which the same information is given in more than one form at the same time, such as spoken narration together with matching on-screen text. In this context, it can support learning by reinforcing information across modalities.",
